# Optional: "Sign in with GitHub" as an alternative to pasting a token.
# Without these the app works the same, with only the token field.
#
# 1. Create an OAuth App: https://github.com/settings/applications/new
#    - Homepage URL:               http://localhost:3000 (or your deployment)
#    - Authorization callback URL: http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback
#    One OAuth App allows a single callback URL, so use a separate app per environment.
# 2. Copy this file to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in both values;
#    on Vercel, set them under Project Settings → Environment Variables.

# Public: inlined into the client bundle to show the sign-in button
NEXT_PUBLIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# Secret: only read by the /api/auth routes on the server
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
